GAL16V8
bbadapt

CLK  INHREQ RO    NC    RI    EN    PAGE  NIB   NC    GND
NC   NC     NC    NC    INH   MATCH OE245 DIR   NC    VCC


;
; Breadboard adapter Board A (backplane adapter) glue logic for an ATF16V8C-7PU
; (7.5 ns max, input to combinational output). Unused inputs (pins 4, 9, 11) are tied
; to GND on the board; pin 4 (PD) carries no signal so the power-down feature can never
; be triggered. Unused I/O pins 12, 13, 14, and 19 are not connected: the ATF16V8C's
; built-in input and I/O pin keepers hold them at their last level, so they never float
; (datasheet, "Input and I/O Pin Keeper Circuits").
;
; Compile with galette. Keep each equation on one line; galette rejects a continuation
; line that starts with "+".
;
; Pin 1 carries the backplane 8 MHz clock but no equation uses it today. It is there so
; registered outputs can be added later with a PLD change only. In registered mode
; pin 1 becomes the dedicated register clock (it no longer reaches the logic array)
; and pin 11 becomes the registered-output enable, which is already tied low. INH,
; DIR, OE245, and MATCH must stay combinational: they act within the same CPU cycle.
;
; Inputs:
;   INHREQ  INH request from the breadboard, active high (10k pulldown on Board A)
;   RO, RI  RAM output / input strobes from the backplane, active low
;   EN      enable switch, active low (switch open = adapter disabled)
;   PAGE    74HC688 U1 match of A8..A15 == $FE, active low
;   NIB     74HC688 U2 match of A4..A7 == DIP switch, active low
;

;
; Match exported to the cable: the 16-byte window ($FE page and the DIP-switch nibble).
;

/MATCH = /PAGE * /NIB

;
; Data 74AHCT245 (U4) output enable: on a window match, and never while the adapter is
; disabled. INH (below) is only asserted inside the window, so this one term also covers
; every cycle where INH is asserted.
;

/OE245 = /EN * /PAGE * /NIB

;
; 74AHCT245 direction (high = cable to backplane) and INH to the backplane: only while
; the breadboard requests INH during a CPU read (RO low, RI high) and the adapter is
; enabled. A breadboard that raises INH request at the wrong time can neither fight the
; CPU on the backplane bus nor inhibit RAM outside a read. Same qualification as the
; timer card's INH. INH and DIR are separate pins with the same equation so the
; off-board INH trace does not share a driver with the local DIR pin. Disabled (EN high)
; drives INH low.
;
; The local window match (/PAGE * /NIB) is part of the term so INH and DIR fall as soon
; as the address leaves the window, without waiting for the breadboard to drop INH
; request over the cable. INH drives the Minimal's SRAM ~CE directly, and every read step
; is followed by an opcode fetch from RAM, so a slow INH release eats into that fetch's
; access time. It adds nothing on assertion: the breadboard cannot raise INH request
; before it has seen ~MATCH.
;

DIR = INHREQ * /RO * RI * /EN * /PAGE * /NIB

INH = INHREQ * /RO * RI * /EN * /PAGE * /NIB

DESCRIPTION

Glue logic for the Minimal 64x4 breadboard adapter, Board A (backplane adapter).
